repository-code: "https://github.com/creelie/ErdosProblem1"
keywords:
  - Erdős–Straus conjecture
  - Egyptian fractions
  - sieve methods
  - Euler totient function
  - large sieve
  - exceptional set
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  We prove that the integers up to N for which the Erdős–Straus equation has
  no solution number at most N exp(-(c0 - eps)(log N)^(2/3)) with the explicit
  constant c0 = 9/(2^(8/3) pi^(2/3)) = 0.6607..., and that this is the best
  constant the large sieve gives with the residue classes used. We also find
  the full asymptotic expansion, with a power-saving error term, of the
  weighted count of search pairs that controls a recent sieve bound for the
  equation; its first two terms were found earlier by Liu.
